  "notes": "Hand-placed on 2026-09-01 (thaikit-model, second build). The derivation cannot clear promote's gate on this prop at any part count: the courtyard wall is a closed ring, so every voxel layer's mask fills solid and the compound stands 4-9 m above the open courtyard (overshoot 0.69 at 8, 16 and 24 parts, coverage 0.9346 in all three). Eight parts by hand: the four wall runs (the front one split at the gate's 1.25 m doorway so the gate is walkable), the hall as one box to the DECK level 5.06 so the roof is standable and the parapet ring is undershoot rather than float, the drum and dome lip as one cylinder to 7.25, and the minaret to its balcony rail at 9.72. The loggia is inside the hall box -- a level builder cannot walk into it at this part ceiling; the domes above 7.25 and the corner domes are undershoot, which the gate does not penalise. Every box is padded one voxel (0.13 m) outward, because the voxeliser marks the cell a face plane touches and an exact-section box leaves a one-cell strip of \"truth\" along every wall uncovered -- 6.5% of this footprint at 0.9246 coverage before the pad.",
